 ],
 "literal": "To kings, permanence is just governance; if that is not there, not enduring will become to kings the glory.",
 "translation": "For kings, permanence of rule comes from a just sceptre; if that is lacking, their glory will not endure.",
 "modern": "மன்னர்களுக்கு நிலைத்தன்மை தருவது நேர்மையான ஆட்சிமுறை ஆகும்; அது இல்லாவிட்டால், மன்னர்களுடைய புகழானது நிலைபெறாமல் அழியும்.",
 "explanation": "This couplet explains that the stability of a king's reign depends entirely on just governance (செங்கோன்மை). The word 'மன்னுதல்' means enduring or remaining stable. If a ruler lacks a just sceptre, their 'ஒளி' (glory or fame) will not last ('மன்னாவாம்'). Thus, the poet emphasizes that justice is the sole foundation of a ruler's lasting reputation and authority.",
